content.text:
Both fixes are now running in the background, one subagent per PR worktree.

- **The decisions are saved:** a new memory file plus a line at the top of the memory index, so they survive compaction. The memory-server save the compaction hook asked for wasn't possible, because that server isn't connecting.
- **#1745:**
  - classify Matter uses by the reader that took them first;
  - run the PIN fallback only when the lock itself reported a PIN;
  - keep a restored event type in the entity's list of event types after a restart;
  - fix the docstring, the `BLUEPRINTS.md` line and the acronyms;
  - use the enum names instead of bare numbers.
- **#1753:**
  - add a dedicated "single read unavailable" error that alone falls back to reading every user;
  - treat a `userIndex` below 1 as no user, and search by `credentialIndex` when the named slot reads empty;
  - unify the two test stubs, and fix the stale docstring and the acronym.

Each subagent will add tests against the fake lock, run mutation checks, cover every changed line, update its PR body before pushing, and post no comments. Once both report back, I'll review the diffs, run `/code-review` on both PRs again, and then draft the reply to owine for you to approve.

