I couldn't do the mempalace checkpoint: mcphub-core is refusing connections this session. Instead I saved this round's decisions to local memory, in `project_matter_use_classification_and_single_read.md`:
- the limiter counts PIN uses only;
- #1753 parses `GetUser` itself;
- the write-path lookup is follow-up #1756;
- the open `event_types` question;
- the #1754 core research.

Both fix rounds are still running in the background. The open question from my last message still needs your answer before the follow-up PR starts. Should `event_types` come from (a) capabilities only, or (b) capabilities plus the recorded fallback? I lean (a).

