    "failure_scenario": "The event carries userIndex=5, and user 5 is untagged (or missing from the fresh read, for example deleted between the event and the read), with credentialType=1 at credentialIndex=3. The lookup returns None and placeable_by_pin_index is True, so the fallback walks PIN index 3 and credits whichever LCM user holds it, even though the lock said user 5 made the use. Fix: gate the fallback on `user_index is None`, which is what the docstrings describe."
  },
  {
    "file": "blueprints/automation/lock_code_manager/slot_usage_notifier.yaml",
    "line": 5,
    "summary": "The notifier's description still says it runs when a code slot PIN is used (line 5, line 12 \"PIN used on lock\", and the line 152 comment \"real PIN uses\"), but it now fires on rfid, fingerprint and face uses too. The PR only updated line 33 of this file.",
    "failure_scenario": "A user reading the blueprint description in the Home Assistant UI expects notifications only for PIN entry, then gets one for every card or fingerprint unlock, and the description contradicts the `credential_type` bullet a few lines below it."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/event.py",
    "line": 223,
    "summary": "Only the last restored kind goes back into `_recorded_types`, so any other recorded kind still drops out of `event_types` after a restart. This is a partial fix, not a fix of the root cause.",
    "failure_scenario": "Slot 1 records an `rfid` use, then a `pin` use, then Home Assistant restarts. The restored event_type is `pin`, so `rfid` is no longer in event_types even though it was proven possible, and the attribute changes across a plain restart. Either persist `_recorded_types` in the entity's extra restore data, or build event_types from what the locks advertise (the follow-up the PR mentions)."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/providers/zigbee2mqtt.py",
    "line": 274,
    "summary": "Zigbee2MQTT maps the source by the `action_source_name` string while ZHA maps the numeric source through `SOURCE_TO_CREDENTIAL_TYPE`. The Zigbee2MQTT payload also carries the numeric `action_source` (the fake bridge publishes both), so there are now two maps for the same Door Lock source values.",
    "failure_scenario": "If a zigbee-herdsman-converters version leaves `action_source_name` out for a source (for example 4), or names it differently, Zigbee2MQTT reports `pin` while ZHA reports `fingerprint` for the same lock, and the two tables can drift. Fix: key Zigbee2MQTT on `action_source` through one shared numeric map."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/providers/zigbee2mqtt.py",
    "line": 60,
    "summary": "This breaks the AGENTS.md rule \"**Spell out acronyms** in code comments instead of using abbreviations.\" (CLAUDE.md says to follow AGENTS.md.) New comments use bare acronyms, while the same PR spells them out elsewhere (zha.py, the `_kind_used` docstring).",
    "failure_scenario": "zigbee2mqtt.py:60 `# source -- keypad, rf, manual -- reports PIN, as it always has.`; matter.py:1903 `# A keypad use is a PIN whatever the lock typed it, but only an index` / `the lock typed as a PIN is a PIN index`; matter.py ~1888 `(a PIN-and-fingerprint user, say)`. The zigbee2mqtt.py:60 line also narrates history (\"as it always has\") instead of stating intent."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/providers/matter.py",
    "line": 1906,
    "summary": "The `credentialType == kPin` check appears twice: once in the `next(...)` that picks the credential (line 1893) and again in `placeable_by_pin_index` (line 1909).",
    "failure_scenario": "The two checks have to stay in step; a future change to one (for example accepting a string \"1\") would leave the other behind, so the chosen credential and the fallback gate would disagree. Simpler: compute `pin_typed = next((pair for pair in used if ... == kPin), None)` once, and derive both the chosen pair and `placeable_by_pin_index = pin_typed is not None and pin_typed[0] is CredentialType.PIN and credential_index is not None` from it."
  }
]
```

